-- A month's salary by the law (MMS-525): what the salary calculator asks.
-- The client, 2026-10-22: "if a teacher wants to know his salary he wants
-- to know the law, he doesn't care about the underlying documents."
--
-- The takanon's §1.1 says what a teaching employee's salary is made of
-- (`salary of a teaching employee`). Here each of those components is
-- the law's answer where the root has one: the root (l4/lib/root.l4) asks
-- every instrument that speaks to the component and applies precedence.
-- A component no pay item of the shared vocabulary stands for yet is
-- §1.1's own figure, and says so (`answered by the root`): the root does
-- not know what the later instruments say about it.
--
-- Two of §1.1's amounts are inputs for a full position: the combined
-- salary (by the salary table, the seniority and the grade) and the 1994
-- supplement. Where the root answers them — the reform's tables give a
-- teacher of Ofek Hadash his combined salary — the month §1.1 computes on
-- is `the month by the law`, with the law's amounts in their place, and
-- every component and allowance §1.1 computes on that month. Where it does
-- not, the input stands, and the page says why the law has no answer
-- (`why the item has no answer in the month`).
--
-- The role allowances the root answers (the pedagogical coordinator's, the
-- mentor's, the junior-division head's) are §1.1ו's allowances, and those
-- of the roles the case holds are the month's too, as many as the cap on
-- role allowances pays (`the role allowances by the law`).
--
-- Beside §1.1's components the month adds the pay items §1.1 does not list
-- and the root answers (`the items the month adds`): the Ofek 2022
-- supplement of a teacher of the reform from 1.9.2022 (the wage agreement of
-- 19.10.2022, §5), in proportion to the position as its §5.3 says, and in
-- §1.1ו's base, since its §5.4 counts it in the percentage supplements
-- computed on the combined salary.
--
-- Nothing here re-encodes a rule: §1.1's components are §1.1's functions,
-- and the law's answer is the root's.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `root`
IMPORT `takanon-1-1`
IMPORT `tables-in-force-common`
IMPORT `2022-10-19_ofek-hadash_wage-agreement`

§ `השכר לחודש לפי הדין`

§§ `המקרה`

-- The case the root is asked about, for a salary month as §1.1 describes
-- it: the month, the 5% step's population and the two amounts §1.1
-- computes come from the month, so that the form asks each fact once.
-- "תוספת 2001" is §1.1's 3% supplement, as §1.1ד reads it. The December
-- 2007 values are asked for a full position, and the month takes them at
-- its own position, as it takes the combined salary (MMS-518): the
-- agreements that compute the 2008 supplement on them (21.2.2008 §4(ט),
-- 24.1.2008 §4(ח)) price the components at December 2007's value, which
-- is a price, not the position of December 2007.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case` @desc the facts of the case §1.1 does not ask about
      m IS A `salary month` @desc the salary month, as §1.1 describes it
GIVETH A `teaching case`
DECIDE `the case of the month` c m IS
    `teaching case` WITH
        `the salary month`                IS m's `month`
        `employer`                        IS c's `employer`
        `in post-primary education`       IS c's `in post-primary education`
        `in the upper division`           IS c's `in the upper division`
        `represented by the secondary teachers' organisation` IS c's `represented by the secondary teachers' organisation`
        `in a population whose 5% step was put off` IS m's `in a population whose 5% step was postponed`
        `combined salary today`           IS `combined salary` m
        `supplement 2001 today`           IS `3% supplement` m
        `supplement 2008 today`           IS `2008 supplement` m
        `combined salary in December 2007` IS c's `combined salary in December 2007` TIMES m's `position fraction of the month`
        `supplement 2001 in December 2007` IS c's `supplement 2001 in December 2007` TIMES m's `position fraction of the month`
        `the kind of school`               IS c's `the kind of school`
        `holds the pedagogical coordinator's role` IS c's `holds the pedagogical coordinator's role`
        `the interns the teacher mentors`  IS c's `the interns the teacher mentors`
        `heads the junior division`        IS c's `heads the junior division`
        `the classes in each grade`        IS c's `the classes in each grade`
        `the roles the teacher holds`      IS c's `the roles the teacher holds`
        `a further role approved by the district manager` IS c's `a further role approved by the district manager`
        `paid by the Ofek Hadash tables`  IS c's `paid by the Ofek Hadash tables`
        `the post in the reform`          IS c's `the post in the reform`
        `the education`                   IS c's `the education`
        `the seniority the tables count`  IS c's `the seniority the tables count`
        `the grade in the tables`         IS c's `the grade in the tables`
        `the school's complexity level`   IS c's `the school's complexity level`

§§ `החודש לפי הדין`

-- An amount §1.1 takes as an input for a full position, as the law gives
-- it: the root's answer where an instrument speaks, else the input. The
-- instruments that speak to these items read the case's placement, never
-- the amounts of the month, so the case is asked of the month as given.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, `the input` IS A NUMBER, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-position amount by the law` i `the input` c m IS
    CONSIDER `the answer that governs` i (`the case of the month` c m)
    WHEN JUST a THEN a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the input`

-- The month §1.1 computes on, with the law's amounts for a full position
-- in place of the inputs.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A `salary month`
DECIDE `the month by the law` c m IS
    `salary month` WITH
        `month`                                       IS m's `month`
        `full-position combined salary`               IS `the full-position amount by the law` `the combined salary of a full position` (m's `full-position combined salary`) c m
        `position fraction of the month`              IS m's `position fraction of the month`
        `is a principal`                              IS m's `is a principal`
        `in a population whose 5% step was postponed` IS m's `in a population whose 5% step was postponed`
        `1994 supplement per full position`           IS `the full-position amount by the law` `the 1994 supplement of a full position` (m's `1994 supplement per full position`) c m

-- The case the root is asked about the month's other items: the month's
-- amounts as the law gives them, and the 2008 supplement the law gives
-- (with the 2001 supplement, the base of the 2011 supplement). No
-- instrument's claim on the 2008 supplement reads it, so it is asked of
-- the case with §1.1's figure in its place. A teacher holds at least the
-- roles the case says he holds of those the root pays an allowance for
-- (`the case holds the role of`): the roles counted are never fewer.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A `teaching case`
DECIDE `the case by the law` c m IS
    `the case with the 2008 supplement and the roles held` k
        (CONSIDER `the answer that governs` `the 2008 public-sector supplement` k
         WHEN JUST a THEN a
         WHEN NOTHING THEN k's `supplement 2008 today`)
    WHERE
        k MEANS `the case of the month` c (`the month by the law` c m)

GIVEN k IS A `teaching case`, a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `teaching case`
DECIDE `the case with the 2008 supplement and the roles held` k a IS
    `teaching case` WITH
        `the salary month`                IS k's `the salary month`
        `employer`                        IS k's `employer`
        `in post-primary education`       IS k's `in post-primary education`
        `in the upper division`           IS k's `in the upper division`
        `represented by the secondary teachers' organisation` IS k's `represented by the secondary teachers' organisation`
        `in a population whose 5% step was put off` IS k's `in a population whose 5% step was put off`
        `combined salary today`           IS k's `combined salary today`
        `supplement 2001 today`           IS k's `supplement 2001 today`
        `supplement 2008 today`           IS a
        `combined salary in December 2007` IS k's `combined salary in December 2007`
        `supplement 2001 in December 2007` IS k's `supplement 2001 in December 2007`
        `the kind of school`               IS k's `the kind of school`
        `holds the pedagogical coordinator's role` IS k's `holds the pedagogical coordinator's role`
        `the interns the teacher mentors`  IS k's `the interns the teacher mentors`
        `heads the junior division`        IS k's `heads the junior division`
        `the classes in each grade`        IS k's `the classes in each grade`
        `the roles the teacher holds`      IS max (k's `the roles the teacher holds`) (`the roles held of those the root pays for` k)
        `a further role approved by the district manager` IS k's `a further role approved by the district manager`
        `paid by the Ofek Hadash tables`  IS k's `paid by the Ofek Hadash tables`
        `the post in the reform`          IS k's `the post in the reform`
        `the education`                   IS k's `the education`
        `the seniority the tables count`  IS k's `the seniority the tables count`
        `the grade in the tables`         IS k's `the grade in the tables`
        `the school's complexity level`   IS k's `the school's complexity level`

§§ `הרכיבים`

-- §1.1's components, in the text's order (א–ה); the percentage allowances
-- (ו) are computed on them and follow.
`§1.1's components` MEANS
    LIST `the combined salary`, `the 3% supplement`, `the 2008 supplement`,
         `the 2011 supplement`, `the 1994 teaching-agreement supplement`

-- The pay item of the shared vocabulary that a component is, where there
-- is one: the takanon's own claim on the 2008 supplement is §1.1ג's
-- (`the 2008 supplement according to the takanon`).
GIVEN s IS A `salary component`
GIVETH A MAYBE `pay item`
DECIDE `the pay item of` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `the combined salary`                    THEN JUST `the combined salary of a full position`
    WHEN `the 3% supplement`                      THEN JUST `the 3% supplement of 2001`
    WHEN `the 2008 supplement`                    THEN JUST `the 2008 public-sector supplement`
    WHEN `the 2011 supplement`                    THEN JUST `the 2011 public-sector supplement`
    WHEN `the 1994 teaching-agreement supplement` THEN JUST `the 1994 supplement of a full position`

-- An item that is an amount for a full position, which `the month by the
-- law` puts in the month; the others are the component itself.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an amount for a full position` i IF
    i EQUALS `the combined salary of a full position` OR i EQUALS `the 1994 supplement of a full position`

GIVEN s IS A `salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `answered by the root` s IS
    CONSIDER `the pay item of` s
    WHEN JUST i THEN TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- §1.1's own figure for a component.
GIVEN s IS A `salary component`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `§1.1's figure for` s m IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `the combined salary`                    THEN `combined salary` m
    WHEN `the 3% supplement`                      THEN `3% supplement` m
    WHEN `the 2008 supplement`                    THEN `2008 supplement` m
    WHEN `the 2011 supplement`                    THEN `2011 supplement` m
    WHEN `the 1994 teaching-agreement supplement` THEN `1994 supplement` m

@export A component of a teaching employee's salary for a month: the law's answer where the root has one, else section 1.1's figure on the month by the law
GIVEN s IS A `salary component` @desc the component
      c IS A `teaching case` @desc the facts of the case §1.1 does not ask about
      m IS A `salary month` @desc the salary month, as §1.1 describes it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the component that governs` s c m IS
    CONSIDER `the pay item of` s
    WHEN JUST i THEN
        IF `an amount for a full position` i
        THEN `§1.1's figure for` s (`the month by the law` c m)
        ELSE
            -- where no instrument gives the item to this case, §1.1's own
            -- figure is what is left, and it is 0 before §1.1 pays it
            CONSIDER `the answer that governs` i (`the case by the law` c m)
            WHEN JUST a THEN a
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `§1.1's figure for` s (`the month by the law` c m)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `§1.1's figure for` s (`the month by the law` c m)

@export A teaching employee's salary for a month, by the law: section 1.1's components, each the law's answer where the root has one, the pay items the month adds beside them, the percentage allowances held, and the role allowances of the roles the case holds
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case` @desc the facts of the case §1.1 does not ask about
      m IS A `salary month` @desc the salary month, as §1.1 describes it
      `the allowances held` IS A LIST OF `allowance held` @desc the percentage allowances held that month, with their rates
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary that governs` c m `the allowances held` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the component that governs` s c m) `§1.1's components`)
        PLUS `the items the month adds, in the month` c m
        PLUS `the percentage allowances by the law` c m `the allowances held`
        PLUS `the role allowances by the law` c m

-- §1.1ו's base, as the law gives it: the components א–ה the law gives for
-- one full position (§1.1ו's own `base of the percentage allowances` is
-- the same sum of §1.1's figures; for a teacher of the reform those are
-- not the month's — his 2001, 2008, 2011 and '94 supplements are 0), and
-- the items the month adds that count in it, for one full position. The
-- role allowances set as a rate are computed on it too (convention
-- reading.ofek-2022-in-role-allowances, put to the lawyer).
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the base of the percentage allowances by the law` c m IS
    sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the component that governs` s c (`the same month at position` m 1)) `§1.1's components`)
        PLUS sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD `the item in the month` i c (`the same month at position` m 1)) `the items the month adds to §1.1ו's base`)

-- One percentage allowance on that base, scaled to the position as §1.1ו
-- scales it (`percentage allowance amount`'s arithmetic on the law's base).
GIVEN a IS A `percentage allowance`, rate IS A NUMBER, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the percentage allowance by the law` a rate c m IS
    rate TIMES `the base of the percentage allowances by the law` c m
         TIMES (`position factor of` a `at` (m's `position fraction of the month`))

GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`, `the allowances held` IS A LIST OF `allowance held`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the percentage allowances by the law` c m `the allowances held` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN h YIELD `the percentage allowance by the law` (h's `allowance held is`) (h's `allowance held rate`) c m) `the allowances held`)

§§ `מה שהחודש מוסיף על רכיבי סעיף 1.1`

-- The pay items the month by the law adds beside §1.1's components (MMS-555):
-- §1.1 does not list them, and the root answers them.
`the items the month adds` MEANS
    LIST `the Ofek 2022 supplement of a full position`

-- Of these, those §1.1ו's allowances are computed on: the agreement of
-- 19.10.2022 (§5.4) counts the Ofek 2022 supplement in "תוספות אחוזיות
-- המחושבות על בסיס השכר המשולב".
`the items the month adds to §1.1ו's base` MEANS
    LIST `the Ofek 2022 supplement of a full position`

-- The Ofek 2022 supplement in the month: the root's answer for a full
-- position, in proportion to the position (the agreement's §5.3, its own
-- `the Ofek 2022 supplement`); 0 where no instrument gives it — before
-- 1.9.2022, off the reform, and to a principal or a first deputy, whose
-- grades the annexes do not price.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ofek 2022 supplement by the law` c m IS
    CONSIDER `the item's answer in the month` `the Ofek 2022 supplement of a full position` c m
    WHEN JUST a THEN `the Ofek 2022 supplement` a (m's `position fraction of the month`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- What an item the month adds comes to in the month; 0 for any other item.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the item in the month` i c m IS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `the Ofek 2022 supplement of a full position` THEN `the Ofek 2022 supplement by the law` c m
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the items the month adds, in the month` c m IS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD `the item in the month` i c m) `the items the month adds`)

§§ `גמולי התפקיד כתוספות אחוזיות`

-- Which of §1.1ו's percentage allowances each role allowance the root
-- answers is (convention reading.role-allowance-kinds, put to the lawyer):
-- the pedagogical coordinator's is a coordination allowance and the
-- mentor's a training allowance (both ו.1, paid as for a full position from
-- a third of one), the junior-division head's a management allowance (ו.1).
-- The number of role allowances paid is a count, no allowance.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A MAYBE `percentage allowance`
DECIDE `the §1.1ו allowance the item is` i c m IS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `the pedagogical coordinator's allowance rate` THEN JUST `subject, laboratory, grade-level and social coordination`
    WHEN `the mentor's allowance rate` THEN JUST `training`
    WHEN `the junior-division head's allowance` THEN JUST `management`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- An item that is a rate on §1.1ו's base; the junior-division head's
-- allowance is in shekels, the root's answer already on the combined
-- salary of the position.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the item is a rate` i IF
    i EQUALS `the pedagogical coordinator's allowance rate` OR i EQUALS `the mentor's allowance rate`

-- What the item comes to in the month as the §1.1ו allowance it is, the
-- role held or not: a rate on §1.1ו's base as the law gives it, scaled to
-- the position as §1.1ו scales that allowance; or, for an allowance in
-- shekels, the root's answer for a full position, scaled the same way (a
-- ו.1 allowance is paid as for a full position from a third of one).
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the item as a percentage allowance in the month` i c m IS
    CONSIDER `the §1.1ו allowance the item is` i c m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        IF `the item is a rate` i
        THEN CONSIDER `the item's answer in the month` i c m
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`the percentage allowance by the law` a v c m)
        ELSE CONSIDER `the item's answer in the month` i c (`the same month at position` m 1)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (v TIMES (`position factor of` a `at` (m's `position fraction of the month`)))

§§ `גמולי התפקיד שהמקרה מחזיק`

-- The role allowances the case holds are the month's (convention
-- reading.role-allowances-in-the-month, put to the lawyer): each role the
-- case holds (`the case holds the role of`) is paid what the item comes to
-- in the month as the §1.1ו allowance it is. §39(ב) of the base agreement
-- caps how many role allowances are paid (the agreement of 19.3.2017 §3(ו)
-- applies it to the mentor's and the pedagogical coordinator's), and the
-- root answers how many (`the role allowances counted`): the roles the case
-- counts beyond these, whose allowances the form lists among §1.1ו's, are
-- taken as paid as listed and fill their places first; the places left go
-- to the roles held here, the highest first (convention amounts.highest).
@desc A role allowance the case holds, and what it comes to in the month.
DECLARE `role allowance in the month` HAS
    `the role's item`   IS A `pay item`
    `the role's amount` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A LIST OF `role allowance in the month`
DECIDE `the role allowances held in the month` c m IS
    concat (map (GIVEN i YIELD
                    IF `the case holds the role of` i c
                    THEN CONSIDER `the item as a percentage allowance in the month` i c m
                         WHEN JUST v THEN LIST (`role allowance in the month` WITH `the role's item` IS i, `the role's amount` IS v)
                         WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
                    ELSE EMPTY)
                `the items a held role pays`)

-- How many of the roles held here the cap leaves places for: the number the
-- root counts, less the case's other roles (taken as paid first); all of
-- them where nothing counts.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the places the cap leaves the roles held` c m IS
    max 0 (`counted` MINUS `the other roles`)
    WHERE
        `held` MEANS `the roles held of those the root pays for` c
        `the other roles` MEANS max 0 (c's `the roles the teacher holds` MINUS `held`)
        `counted` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the answer that governs` `the role allowances counted` (`the case by the law` c m)
            WHEN JUST n THEN n
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `held` PLUS `the other roles`

GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A LIST OF `role allowance in the month`
DECIDE `the role allowances paid in the month` c m IS
    take (`the places the cap leaves the roles held` c m)
         (sortBy (GIVEN a, b YIELD a's `the role's amount` AT LEAST b's `the role's amount`)
                 (`the role allowances held in the month` c m))

GIVEN c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the role allowances by the law` c m IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the role's amount`) (`the role allowances paid in the month` c m))

-- One role's allowance in the month, as the page shows it: what it comes to
-- if the case holds it and the cap pays it, else 0; and whether the case
-- holds it.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the role allowance paid in the month` i c m IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the role's amount`)
             (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the role's item` EQUALS i) (`the role allowances paid in the month` c m)))

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role is held in the month` i c m IS
    `the case holds the role of` i c

§§ `הנימוק`

-- Why the law gives what it gives for a pay item in the month: its answer,
-- the instrument that governs and the rule of precedence by which it does,
-- and what every instrument that speaks to it says, as the page shows
-- them (a module or title of "" where no instrument speaks).
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the item's answer in the month` i c m IS
    `the answer that governs` i (`the case by the law` c m)

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the module that governs the item` i c m IS
    CONSIDER `the ruling on the item` i (`the case by the law` c m)
    WHEN JUST r THEN r's `governed by`'s `module`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN ""

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the title that governs the item` i c m IS
    CONSIDER `the ruling on the item` i (`the case by the law` c m)
    WHEN JUST r THEN r's `governed by`'s `title`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN ""

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the rule that governs the item` i c m IS
    CONSIDER `the ruling on the item` i (`the case by the law` c m)
    WHEN JUST r THEN r's `by the rule`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN ""

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the modules that speak to the item` i c m IS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `by`'s `module`) (`the claims on` i (`the case by the law` c m))

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the titles that speak to the item` i c m IS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `by`'s `title`) (`the claims on` i (`the case by the law` c m))

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `what each says of the item` i c m IS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `answer`) (`the claims on` i (`the case by the law` c m))

-- Why the law gives no answer for an item in the month, as the page says
-- it: "" where it gives one, or where nothing says why.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, k IS A `teaching case`
GIVETH A MAYBE `why there is no answer`
DECIDE `why the law gives no answer on` i k IS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `the combined salary of a full position` THEN `why the Ofek Hadash tables give no combined salary` k
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `why the item has no answer in the month` i c m IS
    CONSIDER `why the law gives no answer on` i (`the case by the law` c m)
    WHEN JUST w THEN `what the gap says` w
    WHEN NOTHING THEN ""

-- Whether the instruments that speak give the case two or more answers.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the item is contradicted in the month` i c m IF
    NOT null (`the contradictions on` i (`the case by the law` c m))
